# A present reference declaration holding nothing -- `@: box Model 0`, the flat name-requirement-value form -- followed
# by a field read, is the implicit `interpreter` throw in both modes, taken by `catch: interpreter ()`
# (l2_own_nullable_root: the one classification of a reference binding that may hold nothing): at the root through the
# working value (`box\v`), and from a native method through the reference-field step of `node\box\v`, which reads the
# cell itself.  The declaration's storage is a typed pointer cell in the root's slot (q26), not a direct Structure
# slot: that cell holding null is the valid nothing; the cell ABSENT from its slot, or the slot holding something that
# is not a pointer cell, is a broken promise of the construction -- X1 at the first read of the cell
# (lmx_pointer_value_promised: "a reference slot holds no pointer cell"), never this throw (the driver's null-path /
# swap-root-fields mutants beside this row).  Entry 7: 1 + 2 (the root read threw) + 4 (the method's read threw); a
# read answering Model's 11 instead leaves 11 in the code.
Model:
    int: v 11
end: Model
@: box Model 0
fn: throughBox () int
    int: got 0
    ---
        got: node\box\v
    ---
    catch: interpreter ()
        got: 4
    return: got
int: code 1
---
    code: box\v
---
catch: interpreter ()
    code: code + 2
code: code + throughBox()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
